  <article class="cr-feature">
    <div>
      <span class="cr-index">03 / APPLY</span>
      <h2>Write code and review it against the same rules.</h2>
      <p>Agents write new code with the rules and validate existing code against them. Code Rules assembles the rules; it does not prescribe how you apply or enforce them. Use any agent harness, skill, custom workflow, or other tool.</p>
      <a href="/for-agents/">See how agents use rules →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cr-panel">
      <span class="cr-index">THE SAME RULE, FROM BUILD TO REVIEW</span>
      <div class="cr-rule"><small>RULE</small><p>Test that requests stop at the retry limit.</p></div>
      <div class="cr-rule"><small>DURING IMPLEMENTATION</small><p>The agent adds a test that fails every attempt and checks that requests stop at the configured limit.</p></div>
      <div class="cr-rule"><small>DURING VALIDATION</small><p>A reviewing agent checks that the test covers the limit and would catch an extra retry.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>
